  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-patoti-tanah-grogot-red-wild-type-bettas",
      "html": "<ul><li>From the Betta unimaculata complex.</li><li>IUCN Red List: Endangered (a very high risk of extinction in the wild).</li><li>Wild caught, from Tanah Grogot.</li><li>Maximum size: 3.5 inches (about 9 cm).</li><li>Breeding: mouthbrooder.</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-patoti-tanah-grogot-red-wild-type-bettas",
      "html": "<ul><li>TDS: ~60–100</li><li>pH: 5.0–7.0</li><li>Temperature: 72–82°F (22–28°C); they prefer cooler temperatures, but higher temperatures induce coloration and breeding behaviour.</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-patoti-tanah-grogot-red-wild-type-bettas",
      "html": "<p>Carnivorous. Fed on live, frozen and dried foods: blackworms, frozen bloodworms and pellets.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-patoti-tanah-grogot-red-wild-type-bettas",
      "html": "<p>Like many of the species in this complex, with the largest bettas, they can be aggressive. They should be kept in a species-only tank, as they can eat anything that fits in their big mouth.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "dimorphism",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-patoti-tanah-grogot-red-wild-type-bettas",
      "html": "<p>Females have less iridescence. Fully grown adult males have longer ventral fins.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-patoti-tanah-grogot-red-wild-type-bettas",
      "html": "<p>Mouthbrooder.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-patoti-tanah-grogot-red-wild-type-bettas",
      "html": "<p>They have a brown base body with blue iridescence on the opercular cheeks, body and tail; females have less iridescence. Both males and females can occasionally show tiger-like stripes on the sides of the body. Fully grown adult males have longer ventral fins. This specific type has a more reddish body than the normal type.</p>"
    }
  ],
